---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../site.config';
import { DOMAINS } from '../lib/domains';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<Base title={`About ${SITE.name}`} current="about">
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>{SITE.description}</p>
    <p>Every morning a script reads the feeds below, drops anything it has seen before, and asks a language model to score each new item for depth, novelty and usefulness to a specific reader. The top dozen get a short summary and a line on why the original is worth opening. Everything links out. Nothing here is original reporting, and the model can be wrong, so read the source before you repeat a claim.</p>
    <h2>Subscribe</h2>
    <p>Each field has its own RSS feed, which works with NetNewsWire, Reeder, Feedly and any other reader, and gives you a home screen widget on iPhone for free:</p>
    <ul>
      {DOMAINS.map((d) => <li><a href={`${base}/${d.slug}/rss.xml`}>{d.name}</a> <code>{`${Astro.site ?? ''}${base}/${d.slug}/rss.xml`.replace(/\/\/+/g, '/').replace(':/', '://')}</code></li>)}
    </ul>
    <p>On iPhone, open a field and use Share → Add to Home Screen to get it as an app.</p>
    {DOMAINS.map((d) => (
      <>
        <h2>{d.name} sources</h2>
        <ul>{d.feeds.map((f) => <li><a href={f.url}>{f.name}</a> <small>({f.kind})</small></li>)}</ul>
      </>
    ))}
  </div>
</Base>
